ECM Simple Implementation
======================================================================
  N has 303 digits
  Trying ECM with various sigmas and B1 values

Simpler approach: P-1 with B1 = 1e9 on N (not M(1237) directly)
  Since F1 is already known, we want to factor N = M(p)/F1.
  P-1 on N: for base a = 3, compute a^(e) mod N where e = prod of prime powers <= B1.
  Then gcd(a^e - 1, N) might give a factor.
  B1 = 1000000000
  Sieving primes up to 1000000000...
